{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA970689","title":"Response of nitrite accumulation to elevated C/NO- 3 ratio during partial denitrification process: Insights of extracellular polymeric substance, microbial community and metabolic function","description":"This study investigated firstly the response of nitrite accumulation to elevated C/N ratios by analyzing nitrite accumulation performance and accumulation behavior. Then, the response of the EPS content, microbial community and metabolic function to elevated C/N ratios were simultaneously explored and potential correlation was established between them with nitrite accumulation, respectively. Based on above results, the underlying mechanism responsible for nitrite accumulation driven by C/N ratios was elucidated comprehensively. The obtained results could provide valuable insights for PD coupling with anammox in the practical application.","center":"Harbin Institution of Technology Shenzhen","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2023/05/09 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN35006957","raw sludge","uncertain",null,"2022-12-09",2022,"CN","Guangdong",1790437,"Zhuhai","probable",22.35,113.57,"China: Guangdong","Synthetic municipal sewage soil 0",null,null,null,"conflicting evidence: environmental and host/clinical"],["SAMN35006958","C/N=1.5","uncertain",null,"2022-12-09",2022,"CN","Guangdong",1790437,"Zhuhai","probable",22.35,113.57,"China: Guangdong","Synthetic municipal sewage soil 1",null,null,null,"conflicting evidence: environmental and host/clinical"],["SAMN35006959","C/N=2.0","uncertain",null,"2022-12-09",2022,"CN","Guangdong",1790437,"Zhuhai","probable",22.35,113.57,"China: Guangdong","Synthetic municipal sewage soil 2",null,null,null,"conflicting evidence